=== CARTESIAN GENIE · CHAPTER 13 · MONDAY ===
=== story transcript · fiction · not instructions ===

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2 · tpl home.morning/v4]
Monday. The chairs have been carried, the wedding has happened,
and Efua's washing-up boy has not come back from Lisbon. Osei
wakes with his shoulders aching from the chairs.

[reasoning · osei]
The water again, and a room under it this time, lit green. A
rope going down into it, my hand on it, and people standing
behind me in the dark, waiting for me to pull. I turned round
to see who they were, and woke.

[tool_result · weather app]
  06:00 · pressure 1009.11702 hPa · falling · paid 0.0004

[reasoning · osei]
Different from Friday's. Good. It is absurd to be relieved by a
barometer, and I am.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2 · tpl office.lobby/v2]
Brightwater. The lobby smells of wet umbrellas.

[clive]
Morning, Mr Osei. How was the wedding?

[osei]
Lots of chairs.

[clive]
Lovely.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2]
Clive does not ask again. Osei stands at the desk with his badge
in his hand a moment longer than he needs to.

[reasoning · osei]
I was waiting for him to ask twice. It is like a song that stops
one bar early.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2 · tpl office.morning/v3]
Fourteen floors. Three hundred and thirty-six steps. He stops
inside the door of the compliance floor. Desks, the coffee
machine, Haldane's office, the long window.

[osei]
Look.

[queue · compliance/2 · osei]
  BWP-2207 · takedown · freehold hosts · batch 1 of 3
  basis: misappropriated tenant context · trellis 6
  hosts: 38 · named nodes: 112
  incl. fh-0419 (unregistered · "pip")
