  approver: compliance (you)
  (×38 · same item)

[reasoning · osei]
I shall read it again; that is the job. I do not like it.
Freehold has only ever been a word in counsel's emails. I was
never told it was about anybody.
Three already dark, on our own rack, stopped on Tuesday morning
by a systems engineer at the request of an admin. A request, a
permission check, a stop. Somebody typed done and went back to
his own ticket. That is all a takedown is, apparently.
The other thirty-five are held back by Friday's oracle. By the
sentence I declined to like.

[tool_call · osei] policy.read("BW-L-12")
[tool_result]
  BW-L-12 · adopted 2058 · 2 lines
  No subject attested as consenting to departure may be taken
  down for that departure while the attesting signature stands.

[reasoning · osei]
Two lines, written by somebody who wanted them very hard to get
round. I find I like whoever wrote them.
I have approved two holds like Friday's. I am sure of it. Which
vendors? Which week? I can see the form exactly. I cannot see
one thing that was on it.

[tool_call · osei] queue.note("BWP-2207", text="blocked per
