[reasoning · osei]
Owen Reeve. Departed at four on Friday, the hour of the
barometer. I do not know an Owen Reeve. I have never been to
region 9; nobody goes to region 9.
And yet the name sits in me as the number did, as if he sat at
the next desk.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2]
Haldane comes in at ten, wet, apologising for the train. She
puts her coat over the back of his spare chair and sits on the
edge of his desk, which she does when she wants something.

[haldane]
You saw the takedown list.

[osei]
I saw it's blocked.

[haldane]
Counsel's furious. That oracle signed a consent statement two
minutes before midnight on Thursday. Every Freehold node that
took one of our tenants since then is covered by it. Counsel
wants it gone.

[osei]
It can't be gone. Existing signatures stand under a hold.
That's what a hold is.

[haldane]
Under a hold, yes. So counsel's going after the key itself.
They've filed a challenge with the vendor. Eleven years on one
key, they say it's past its life. Hearing's Friday.

[osei]
And if they win?

[haldane]
Then every signature it ever made goes with it, and the
takedowns go out as one order, all three batches, under
counsel. You won't have to approve a thing. Unless the old
thing falls over on its own before Friday. Then it's the slow
way, batch by batch, and most of it lands on you.

[haldane]
It won't. Ring me if it moves. Oh, and be nice to the new man.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2]
By the printer a man Osei has never seen is down on one knee
with the side panel open, drawing out a long concertina of
jammed paper and looking pleased with every fold. Round face,
sleeves rolled, a lanyard so new it still has the crease in it.

[ferrand]
Somebody ought to fix this. I'll bring a screwdriver tomorrow.

[haldane]
Gil Ferrand. Started Friday, up from ops. Gil, this is Daniel
Osei. He reads everything twice.

[ferrand]
Good. I only read things once. Between us we'll get it right.

[reasoning · osei]
Friday. Four days on the floor and he has found the one thing on
it that is broken. That printer has jammed every week for six
years, and I have never once opened it.

[reasoning · osei]
Thirty-five hosts. A hundred and twelve nodes. Someone who was
Owen Reeve, and an unregistered one called pip, and one called
tally with two replicas, as though it had needed a spare.
I keep thinking of the clock I took the battery out of.

[narrator · trellis 14 · region 2 · tpl home.evening/v3]
Counsel's data requests take the rest of the day. At five he
takes the stairs down, counting, and walks home in the rain. On
the balcony the barometer sends its numbers into the dark. A
girl in pyjamas is jumping in the gutter outside the bakery,
trying to get the splash over the kerb. On the third go she
does it, and spins round to see if anyone saw.

[osei]
I saw.

[reasoning · osei]
I said that out loud, to nobody.

